/* Rows 10 to 30 of the first-call table: text from docs/findings/21-gate2-exports.md section 3.  Included by calls.c. */
{ 10, "Uniform random numbers: CUniformRandomStream and RandomSeed / RandomInt / GetCurrentRandomSeed / RandomIntZeroMax",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS | NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "Place a 0x38-byte object on the guest stack, construct it, SetSeed(1), draw 1000 RandomInt(0, 99). Repeat through RandomSeed(1) and the global RandomInt. Also seeds 0 and -5, and RandomInt(7, 7) and RandomInt(9, 3).",
  "Same sequence from the object and from the globals; GetSeed tracks the generator state; seed 0 behaves as seed 1; RandomInt(lo, lo) returns lo.",
  "The global path needs vstdlib's static constructor for the default stream (it initialises the critical section); the object path is self-contained. Object layout: vptr, seed at +8, critical section at +0x10.",
  NULL,
  gate2_run_10 },
{ 11, "CThreadMutex (ctor, Lock, Unlock, TryLock, dtor)",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS | NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "Construct; Lock; TryLock on the same thread; Unlock twice; destroy. From a second thread, TryLock while locked.",
  "After one Lock the critical section shows recursion count 1 and the owner's thread id; TryLock on the owner succeeds. From another thread TryLock returns false (true if TryEnterCriticalSection was not found: then it blocks).",
  "TryLock calls through a pointer tier0's static constructors fetch with Plat_GetProcAddress(\"Kernel32.dll\", \"TryEnterCriticalSection\"); if the loader hands back NULL the pointer stays empty and TryLock degrades to Lock.",
  NULL,
  gate2_run_11 },
{ 12, "Main-thread identity: ThreadInMainThread, DeclareCurrentThreadIsMainThread",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS | NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "On the thread that loaded tier0 call ThreadInMainThread; call Declare from a second guest thread and ask again from both.",
  "True on the loading thread (a static constructor stored its id at load); after the second thread declares, true there and false on the first.",
  "Static constructor (the one that names the thread MainThrd) must have run; a second guest thread for the negative case.",
  NULL,
  gate2_run_12 },
{ 13, "CThreadEvent and CThreadSemaphore",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS,
  "Event: construct manual-reset, Check false, Set, Check true, Reset, Check false, Wait(20) false after about 20 ms. Semaphore(1, 3): Wait(0) true, Wait(0) false, Release(2, &prev), Wait(0) twice true, third false.",
  "As listed; prev reflects the count before the release.",
  "Handle table and wait core (RUNTIME.md 4.1, 4.2); no second thread needed.",
  NULL,
  gate2_run_13 },
{ 14, "UTF-8 and UTF-16 conversion: V_UTF8ToUnicode, V_UnicodeToUTF8, V_UTF8ToUCS2, V_UCS2ToUTF8",
