  NULL,
  gate2_run_15 },
{ 16, "Plat_gmtime",
  0,
  "Times 0, 86399, 951782400, 1700000000, 32535215999 (the last second of year 3000) and 32535291599 (the last the C runtime accepts); then 32535291600, 253402300799 and 2^62; out is a 36-byte buffer of nine ints. (Corrected 2026-10-10: the finding listed 253402300799 as valid.) Then -1824522369, the time the reference run of 2026-10-10 passed to the real DLL (docs/handoff/ref-rank16.md), and -1, -43200, -43201, whose results are recorded and not expected.",
  "For the accepted times tm_sec, tm_min, tm_hour, tm_mday, tm_mon, tm_year, tm_wday, tm_yday, tm_isdst equal the host gmtime_r values (tm_year = year - 1900); the three later times return EINVAL (22). -1824522369 returns EINVAL with the nine fields set to -1.",
  "Pure calendar arithmetic in the C runtime, but _gmtime64_s begins with a 36-byte memset (tier0 RVA 0x25bd0), which the lifter skips today (movnti): blocked until that is lifted. The invalid-argument path also reaches _errno and the unlifted FLS wrappers (section 5).",
  "tier0+0x25bd0 memset (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x2ad80 FLS/TLS wrapper: get value (jmp rax); tier0+0x2ad9c FLS/TLS wrapper: set value (jmp rax)",
  run_16 },
{ 17, "CommandLine() and the CCommandLine object",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS | NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "CreateCmdLine(\"game.exe -foo 5 +bar baz -neg -3\"); GetCmdLine; ParmCount; FindParm(\"-foo\"), FindParm(\"-FOO\"), FindParm(\"-nope\"); ParmValue(\"-foo\", 99); ParmValue(\"+bar\", \"x\"); ParmValue(\"-neg\", 7); GetParm(4); GetParm(99).",
  "Count 7; FindParm returns 1, 1 (the compare is case-insensitive: it lower-cases A to Z) and 0; ParmValue(-foo) 5; ParmValue(+bar) \"baz\"; ParmValue(-neg, 7) returns the default 7 (a value starting with + or - is treated as another parm); GetParm(4) \"baz\"; out of range returns an empty string.",
  "CommandLine() returns NULL until two static constructors ran (they initialise the mutex and set a flag). Copies the string with the game allocator, so the allocator is used (see rank 22).",
  "tier0+0x249c0 memmove (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x25bd0 memset (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x2ad80 FLS/TLS wrapper: get value (jmp rax); tier0+0x2ad9c FLS/TLS wrapper: set value (jmp rax)",
  gate2_run_17 },
{ 18, "GetCPUInformation and the clock-speed data exports",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS | NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "Call; read the first dword, the qword at +8, byte flags at +4 to +7 and the processor-count byte. Compare with the data exports.",
  "First dword 0x18; qword at +8 equals g_ClockSpeed (tier0 RVA 0xa9a60) and its low half g_dwClockSpeed; g_ClockSpeedSecondsMultiplier * speed == 1.0 within 1e-9; speed lies between 5e8 and 6e9 (a smaller value means the runtime's rdtsc is not a cycle counter); logical-processor byte matches GetSystemInfo.",
  "Already runs once inside the load: a static constructor calls it and then spins on QueryPerformanceCounter for about 1/32 s while reading rdtsc, so a counter that never advances hangs the load. Needs the lifted rdtsc and cpuid.",
  "tier0+0x25bd0 memset (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x2ad80 FLS/TLS wrapper: get value (jmp rax); tier0+0x2ad9c FLS/TLS wrapper: set value (jmp rax)",
  gate2_run_18 },
{ 19, "Logging channel lookup: LoggingSystem_GetChannelCount, LoggingSystem_FindChannel",
  NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "After load: GetChannelCount; FindChannel(\"General\"), FindChannel(\"general\"), FindChannel(\"LOADING\"), FindChannel(\"nothing\").",
  "Count is at least 2; General and LOADING found with distinct non-negative ids below the count; \"general\" gives the same id as \"General\" (case-insensitive compare, the same routine FindParm uses); the last returns -1.",
  "Needs tier0's entry point to have run (static constructors register the channels). The table is built lazily on first use and registers an atexit handler.",
  "tier0+0x25bd0 memset (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x2ad80 FLS/TLS wrapper: get value (jmp rax); tier0+0x2ad9c FLS/TLS wrapper: set value (jmp rax)",
  gate2_run_19 },
{ 20, "AllocateThreadID / FreeThreadID",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS | NEEDS_TLS | NEEDS_ENTRY,
  "AllocateThreadID, read the TLS value for the index stored in tier0 RVA 0x19a3cc, FreeThreadID, Allocate again.",
  "First id is 1; after Free the next Allocate gives 1 again; a second thread gets 2.",
  "A static constructor allocates the TLS index with TlsAlloc; Error() is the out-of-ids path.",
  NULL,
  gate2_run_20 },
{ 21, "MemAllocScratch / MemFreeScratch",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS,
  "a = Alloc(100); b = Alloc(200); Free; c = Alloc(150); Free; Free. Write a pattern into each block.",
  "b == a + 100; c == b; no overlap; buffer first created with at least 0x800 bytes.",
  "Uses the game allocator (IMemAlloc Alloc and Realloc); first use constructs it (rank 22).",
  NULL,
  gate2_run_21 },
{ 22, "The game allocator: CreateGlobalMemAlloc, IMemAlloc vtable, CAlignedNewDelete operator new / delete",
  NEEDS_IMPORTS,
  "p = CreateGlobalMemAlloc() twice; Alloc(100); GetSize; fill; Realloc to 1000 and check the first 100 bytes; Free; Alloc of 0x900 (large path); operator new(40) and delete.",
  "Same pointer both times; vptr equals tier0 + 0x52fb8; Alloc returns non-null; GetSize >= 100; Realloc preserves contents; operator new returns an 8-byte aligned pointer and delete frees the block it took from.",
  "The first caller builds the allocator in static storage; other threads spin on Sleep until it is published. g_pMemAllocSingleton is NULL until some caller caches it.",
  "tier0+0x249c0 memmove (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x25bd0 memset (C runtime; movnti); tier0+0x25f40 strstr-like search (C runtime; SSE4.2 string compare); tier0+0x2ad80 FLS/TLS wrapper: get value (jmp rax); tier0+0x2ad9c FLS/TLS wrapper: set value (jmp rax)",
  gate2_run_22 },
